kunzite: Adreno 710 step 17, HFI messages to the GMU (kgpu=17; 16's check relaxed, 1-15 unchanged).
16: a word that still reads what it held after the write is "write ignored" (boot #37: the three
hidden TCS command addresses, wired to the PDC's +0x4514/+0x4510/+0x4520), reported, not a failure.
17 does kgsl's gen7_hfi_start after reset_hfi_queues. Tables as gen7_build_rpmh_tables: the ARC
levels of gfx.lvl/cx.lvl/mx.lvl from cmd-db (counted as adreno_rpmh_arc_cmds), the FDT levels of
speed bin 0xc6 (295-940 MHz, qcom,level 56..416, no qcom,cx-level so every dep vote 0xffffffff),
the GMU's 200/500 MHz at LOW_SVS/SVS (no qcom,gmu-freq-table): the legacy H2F_MSG_PERF_TBL
(hfi_dcvstable_cmd, 59 words: HFI 2.1 is before 2.6.1); the BCMs SH0/MC0/ACV and CN0 from cmd-db
(address, unit, width, vcd) with the FDT's qcom,bus-table-ddr7 (ddr_device_type 7) and
bus-table-cnoc, ab 0, ACV perfmode 0x8 above level 0: H2F_MSG_BW_VOTE_TBL (hfi_bwtable_cmd, 160
words). Then H2F_MSG_FEATURE_CTRL for IFPC, ACD and BCL off (kgsl only sends enables; a refusal is
reported) and H2F_MSG_CORE_FW_START. Each command goes into the command queue (cookie-padded to 4
words, seqnum/size in the header), HOST2GMU_INTR_SET 1, then GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO bit 0 or the
message queue moving within 1 s (NMI ends the wait), the ack matched on the sent header, result 0.
The HFI block is accessed through an uncached alias (ml_io_map_unmappable, VM_WIMG_WCOMB; unmapped
before the step returns): the GMU sees it uncached, and its indices share cache lines with ours.
The cmd-db lookup moves out of kg_arc into kg_db_find; step 2 keeps the speed bin. Undo: a second
CM3 reset entry, so the GMU stops before step 16's RSC/PDC words go back (40 entries at most).

